{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01FjLYq6NMqB2ThhPdtX5LFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on `CLAUDE.md` at the workspace root, here's what this project **is**:\n\n- **It's a research sandbox, not a production system.** John Liechty's \"Agentic Sandbox\" / Ghost World Labs (GWL) â€” a workspace for building, training, and evaluating clusters of AI agents. Most of its ~80 root markdown files are design docs (whitepapers, plans, session logs); a smaller subset is runnable code.\n\n- **The shipped deliverable is a Next.js supervisor GUI.** `sandbox-lab-gui/` (the \"GWL-M master GUI\") launches and supervises agents over a custom Next.js + WebSocket server (`server.mjs`), started via `Launch-Ghost-World-Labs.bat` on `http://localhost:3001`. It pre-spawns Gemini CLI, Claude Code, and the Alpha agent terminals, with an Agent Matrix for spawning others.\n\n- **Agents run on the OpenClaw runtime.** A globally-installed MIT-licensed npm package; the GUI dispatches turns to it via `agent-chat.mjs`, with per-agent model/provider routing in `Sandbox Setup Package/config/routing.json`.\n\n- **The current daily-use product is a \"t2r\" two-half brain agent** (`alpha-v0`) â€” a Tasteâ†’Reason dispatcher (`brain/dispatcher/t2r-dispatcher.mjs`) with a 7-skill bundle and a $100/month wallet cap, plus research/legacy agents behind a toggle.\n\n- **The active build front is the \"sovereign t2r harness\"** â€” a brain-agnostic agentic harness (a guarded ReAct loop with cache-stable routing, cost ledgers, tier routing, and verify/approval/replan workers, all default-OFF and flag-gated). The stated design goal: distill from frontier models into small **local** students (QLoRA on â‰¤8B models on the box's RTX 4070), enabling a 3-brain lineup (Opus-4.8 baseline Â· t2r efficient Â· fully-local sovereign).\n\n- **It ships a master skill ecosystem** linked into Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and (by file-copy) OpenClaw from `skills-master/` â€” expert-coder, deep-research, project-manager, research1, etc.\n\nThe current focus (per \"Recently completed\") is a Crucible-forged, Foreman-ready plan to take the harness from its held branch to GA, with the brain work sequenced after.\n\nIf you want, I can verify any of these against the actual code rather than the doc claims (e.g., confirm `server.mjs`, the dispatcher, or the harness files exist)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7051,"cache_read_input_tokens":40827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7051,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e43a3477-7410-4c4a-bc2c-3f49a3b70b35","uuid":"9096a7b8-5d59-4958-b58e-8eafdb32c9e1","request_id":"req_011Cc2N2GLRSYDnR8SVLSXWU"}
